        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 253.41,
          "end": 257.01,
          "en": "the streamBuilder widget provided by Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 257.01,
          "end": 260.25,
          "en": "Now that's a widget we haven't used up to this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 260.25,
          "end": 263.73,
          "en": "but it is quite similar to the future builder widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 263.73,
          "end": 266.013,
          "en": "about which you did learn earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 267.03,
          "end": 271.17,
          "en": "You might recall that FutureBuilder was used to listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 271.17,
          "end": 275.37,
          "en": "to a future and then render different widgets based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 275.37,
          "end": 277.62,
          "en": "on the state of their future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 277.62,
          "end": 279.93,
          "en": "StreamBuilder is quite similar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 279.93,
          "end": 281.85,
          "en": "but the difference between a future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 281.85,
          "end": 286.031,
          "en": "and a stream is that a future in the end will be done once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 286.031,
          "end": 290.19,
          "en": "it resolved, so it'll only ever produce one value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 290.19,
          "end": 294.45,
          "en": "or error, whereas a stream on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 294.45,
          "end": 298.14300000000003,
          "en": "is capable of producing multiple values over time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 299.13,
          "end": 302.88,
          "en": "And StreamBuilder wants a stream value, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 302.88,
          "end": 306.18,
          "en": "and then also a builder function, which will be a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 306.18,
          "end": 309.15,
          "en": "that automatically receives some context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 309.15,
          "end": 311.613,
          "en": "and then also a data snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 312.6,
          "end": 314.91,
          "en": "Now just as with FutureBuilder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 314.91,
          "end": 316.8,
          "en": "this function will be called by Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 316.8,
          "end": 321.36,
          "en": "Whenever the stream will connect here will emit a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 321.36,
          "end": 324.15,
          "en": "and that snapshot in the end will give us access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 324.15,
          "end": 325.743,
          "en": "to that emitted value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 326.7,
          "end": 329.79,
          "en": "Now the stream I want to connect here is coming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 329.79,
          "end": 333.024,
          "en": "from my Firebase off package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 333.024,
          "end": 335.373,
          "en": "And there again from the instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 335.373,
          "end": 339.783,
          "en": "and there we can use the authStateChanges method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 340.68,
          "end": 345.03,
          "en": "And this method, as you can see here, will return a stream.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 345.03,
          "end": 347.31,
          "en": "So in the end here, we set up a listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 347.31,
          "end": 350.723,
          "en": "that's being managed by the Firebase SDK under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 350.723,
          "end": 354.749,
          "en": "And Firebase will emit a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 354.749,
          "end": 358.56,
          "en": "whenever anything auth related changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 358.56,
          "end": 361.327,
          "en": "So for example, if a token becomes available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 361.327,
          "end": 365.28,
          "en": "or if a token is removed because the user was logged out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 365.28,
          "end": 366.273,
          "en": "for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 367.26,
          "end": 370.642,
          "en": "So auth state changes will give us such a stream",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 370.642,
          "end": 373.5,
          "en": "and snapshot, therefore then in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 373.5,
          "end": 377.25,
          "en": "will be a user data package, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 377.25,
          "end": 380.369,
          "en": "created and emitted by Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 380.369,
          "end": 382.41,
          "en": "So here in the builder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 382.41,
          "end": 387.41,
          "en": "we can then check if Snapshot has data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 387.48,
          "end": 390.36,
          "en": "So if we have some user data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 390.36,
          "end": 393.96,
          "en": "and if that's the case, I wanna return my ChatScreen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 393.96,
          "end": 395.61,
          "en": "because that in the end will mean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 395.61,
          "end": 398.13,
          "en": "that we have a locked in user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 398.13,
          "end": 400.77,
          "en": "Because Firebase will not emit any data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 400.77,
          "end": 402.81,
          "en": "if we don't have a locked in user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 402.81,
          "end": 405,
          "en": "so if we don't have a token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 405,
          "end": 407.19,
          "en": "Therefore, as an alternative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
